&lt;h2&gt;


  🛠️ The Tech Stack
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I chose modern, cutting-edge tools to achieve high frame rates and responsive interactions:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React 19 &amp;amp; Vite 8:&lt;/strong&gt; Lightning-fast HMR and modular component architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tailwind CSS v4:&lt;/strong&gt; Modern CSS engine for responsive layouts and glassmorphic styling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Framer Motion 12 &amp;amp; GSAP:&lt;/strong&gt; Smooth spring physics, window transitions, and scroll animations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Lenis:&lt;/strong&gt; Smooth momentum scrolling for narrative pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Vercel &amp;amp; Vercel Analytics:&lt;/strong&gt; Ultra-fast CDN edge hosting and privacy-friendly visitor analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  💡 Key Architectural Features
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  1. The Liquid Glass Dock
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Recreating the macOS dock in CSS requires more than just &lt;code&gt;backdrop-filter: blur()&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;I engineered &lt;strong&gt;SVG displacement filters&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;feTurbulence&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;feDisplacementMap&lt;/code&gt;) to simulate realistic light refraction across the dock's glass surface.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calculated smooth proximity magnification physics (&lt;code&gt;scale: 1.25&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;radius: 95px&lt;/code&gt;) based on pointer coordinates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Added bounce animations on app launch and subtle indicator dots for active background tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. 60 FPS Desktop Widgets
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The desktop features live, interactive Sonoma-style widgets:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Analog Clock:&lt;/strong&gt; Driven by a &lt;code&gt;requestAnimationFrame&lt;/code&gt; render loop with an authentic sweeping orange second hand and multi-timezone cycling (Indore, Cupertino, London, Tokyo).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Calendar Widget:&lt;/strong&gt; Offers real-time date tracking and an interactive monthly agenda view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  3. "My Journey" — The Story Scroller
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of a bulleted resume, the &lt;strong&gt;"My Journey"&lt;/strong&gt; app launches a full-screen, milestone-based interactive roadmap. It animates through career milestones, technical skills, and design philosophies as the user scrolls.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  4. Built-In Apps Ecosystem
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The desktop includes fully functional simulated macOS applications:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Vision Music:&lt;/strong&gt; A custom in-browser audio player with scrubbing, playlist queue, and sound visualization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interactive CLI Terminal:&lt;/strong&gt; A working terminal emulator supporting custom commands (&lt;code&gt;help&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;projects&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;contact&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;clear&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ask Harshit AI:&lt;/strong&gt; Integrated with the &lt;strong&gt;Google Gemini API&lt;/strong&gt; for answering visitor questions about my experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GitHub Explorer &amp;amp; Stats:&lt;/strong&gt; Fetches real-time commit data and repository metrics directly from the GitHub REST API.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Blog &amp;amp; Articles:&lt;/strong&gt; Automatically pulls this DEV.to feed dynamically!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  🧠 Lessons Learned
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;State Management for Windowing:&lt;/strong&gt; Orchestrating multiple draggable, resizable windows (handling z-index focus, minimizes, and maximizes) required a clean centralized state model in React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Performance Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Layering multiple heavy blur filters can hurt GPU performance on mobile devices. Adding graceful fallbacks and CSS &lt;code&gt;will-change&lt;/code&gt; properties kept animations buttery-smooth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




